WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:11.457
Yikes!

2
00:00:11.458 --> 00:00:14.058
Yikes!

3
00:00:14.059 --> 00:00:17.400
Who are you?

4
00:00:17.401 --> 00:00:21.112
I'm an American alligator.

5
00:00:21.113 --> 00:00:25.666
Alligators are large reptiles.

6
00:00:25.667 --> 00:00:28.396
Where do you live?

7
00:00:28.397 --> 00:00:32.352
We live in the United States.

8
00:00:32.353 --> 00:00:35.473
We like warm water.

9
00:00:35.474 --> 00:00:40.527
We swim in rivers, lakes, and swamps.

10
00:00:40.528 --> 00:00:43.517
What do you eat?

11
00:00:43.518 --> 00:00:48.512
We like frogs, fish, snails, and mammals.

12
00:00:48.513 --> 00:00:52.153
Alligators don't chew food.

13
00:00:52.154 --> 00:00:58.836
We just gulp it down!

14
00:00:58.837 --> 00:01:02.317
You have wide jaws.

15
00:01:02.318 --> 00:01:06.586
My jaws are very strong.

16
00:01:06.587 --> 00:01:12.152
I can even crack a turtle's hard shell!

17
00:01:12.153 --> 00:01:18.077
We grab prey with our sharp teeth.

18
00:01:18.078 --> 00:01:21.766
This swamp is noisy!

19
00:01:21.767 --> 00:01:26.929
Alligators hiss loudly.

20
00:01:26.930 --> 00:01:33.926
We can roar like lions too.

21
00:01:33.927 --> 00:01:37.077
Do you hibernate?

22
00:01:37.078 --> 00:01:41.515
No. But we sleep in holes sometimes.

23
00:01:41.516 --> 00:01:45.398
We find a muddy spot in water.

24
00:01:45.399 --> 00:01:49.634
Then we dig holes to keep warm.

25
00:01:49.635 --> 00:01:53.673
Your tail looks powerful!

26
00:01:53.674 --> 00:01:56.785
It is powerful.

27
00:01:56.786 --> 00:02:00.865
My tail moves me through the water.

28
00:02:00.866 --> 00:02:06.592
I love to swim.

29
00:02:06.593 --> 00:02:09.928
I'm getting hungry.

30
00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:13.498
Bye.

31
00:02:13.499 --> 00:02:20.469
See you later, American Alligator!
